[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Dialogue/DialogueChoice.cs" id="3_choice"]

; Bram Corrow (faction.dawnwardens, RankPeerNpcId). Phase 42C.
;
; He carries the whole probation arc so no fact about it has two owners: the offer, the fork, the
; objectives (quest.dawnwardens.probation) and the rank-one grant are all one conversation graph.
; The root keeps the standard member/stranger split (Condition 14/15, rank 0, exhaustive) exactly as
; every other officer's does — he will not discuss guild work with someone who has not joined.
;
; ⚠️ THE FORK IS DECIDED BEFORE THE QUEST EXISTS, the barrels shape (41D / quest.hollowreach.barrels):
; ch_fork_rescue/ch_fork_expedient each set ONE flag and go to a "_go" node whose one choice starts
; the quest (Effect = 1). The two fork choices gate on EACH OTHER (Condition 6, MissingFlag) so a
; player who picks a side and walks off without accepting still has only one door open on return.
; SequentialObjectives on the quest means neither Reach objective can complete before the Defend does,
; regardless of how early the flag is set - the fight is still the fight.
;
; ⚠️ RANK ONE IS GRANTED ONLY ON COMPLETION, NOT ON THE FORK. The branch flag says which way the
; player chose, but it is set BEFORE the quest starts, so it must never gate anything that speaks of
; the corrie in the past tense. The nesting is therefore QuestCompleted OUTSIDE, branch flag INSIDE:
; member offers ch_after (Condition 3) into "after", and only there do ch_claim_rescue/ch_claim_expedient
; (Condition 5, HasFlag) pick the branch, grant rank one and land on after_rescue/after_expedient, whose
; past-tense lines are thus reachable only post-completion, with no compound condition anywhere. Neither branch pays a different reward (the quest's own
; FactionRewardId/Amount, faction.villagers, is one field) - Sedge's header already made that call
; for the same reason: a second place rewards live is invariant 5 waiting to happen. What differs is
; what Bram says, which is the consequence a player actually feels.
;
; ⚠️ NEITHER BRANCH TOUCHES THE IRON KING. The tension is the Dawnwardens' own - civilians first or
; the order kept, Danhal's silent argument with the world - and 42D is the one that gets to spend the
; Iron King's flags on it.
;
; ── Phase 42D — the command arc and its payoff ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; ⚠️ THE WARRANT-RIDER IS FLAVOUR, NOT A GATE. ch_command_iron_alive / ch_command_iron_defeated read
; flag.iron_king_defeated (Condition 5 HasFlag / 6 MissingFlag) purely to pick which of two identical-
; shaped nodes narrates the dispute - both lead into the same command_offer_* text and the same two
; mechanical choices beneath it. Nothing here ever SetFlag/ClearFlag on it: the Build note is explicit
; that this dispute must never gate or consume the main-story flag, and reading it without ever
; writing it is invariant 18's write-side rule applied to a flag family that ISN'T ours to own.
;
; ⚠️ THE ESCORT IS RECRUITED HERE, NOT OUT OF HER OWN CONVERSATION. Sella Ru (companion.dawnwarden_witness)
; has no world body before ch_command_accept fires Effect 5 (RecruitCompanion) - dialogue.iron_client's
; shape (42I), which itself copies Tessa's (41B). One choice, one effect, so starting the quest is a
; second click on command_recruited (Effect 1 StartQuest, no Goto) - rescue_go/expedient_go's shape.
;
; ⚠️ RANK TWO USES SetFlag, NOT GuildRank, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. ch_command_after
; (Condition 3 QuestCompleted quest.dawnwardens.command) stays reachable forever once the command
; quest is done - the same shape "member" already gives ch_probation_active's siblings - so a player
; can revisit it AFTER the finale has already granted rank three. GuildRank ":2" would CLEAR rank
; three on that revisit (it sets exactly the ranks up to its argument and clears anything above,
; 42I's own doc comment on the effect); Effect 2 (SetFlag "guild.dawnwardens.rank2") only ever adds
; the flag, so a late revisit is a no-op instead of a demotion. GuildRank is still the right tool at
; ch_finale_done below, because 3 is this guild's declared ceiling (RankNameKeys.Count) and nothing
; can ever be above it to clear.
;
; ⚠️ THE FINALE FORK IS quest.hollowreach.barrels's SHAPE A THIRD TIME IN ONE ARC. ch_finale_fork_service
; / ch_finale_fork_authority each set one flag and gate on each other's absence (Condition 6,
; MissingFlag) before quest.dawnwardens.finale exists, exactly as the probation fork does two nodes up.
;
; ⚠️ RANK THREE SITS OUTSIDE THE BRANCH; guild.dawnwardens.finale SITS INSIDE IT - probation's nesting
; rule (42C's header) read the other way round, because this time the OUTER fact (rank three) does not
; presuppose which side was taken and the INNER fact (which past-tense line plays, and the finale flag
; that flag.dawnwardens.finale_service/_authority pays into it) does. ch_finale_done therefore carries
; Effect 12 (GuildRank "faction.dawnwardens:3") unconditionally past QuestCompleted; the branch is
; resolved only once more, at ch_claim_service/ch_claim_authority, each Effect 2 (SetFlag
; "guild.dawnwardens.finale") landing on its own past-tense node.

